Manila Barangay Flood Risk Complete Pipeline (Manuscript Ver. 2)

Notebook: Manila_Barangay_Flood_Risk_Pipeline.ipynb
(FEATURE_SPEC = "reduced": 8 predictors retained after the correlation/VIF screen.
Set FEATURE_SPEC = "full" in the decision cell to reproduce the original 11-predictor run.)

Files Needed (Input/)

Because the shape-to-CSV/geospatial processing was completed separately in QGIS, this notebook now requires only tabular inputs:

1. `MetroManila_Barangay_Flood_Area_Validated.csv` — QGIS-prepared flood area and flood percentage table.
2. `population-dataset-2024.csv` — PSA 2024 barangay population estimates.
3. `population-dataset-2020.xlsx` — PSA 2020 barangay population table.
4. `manila_final_base_dataset_NEW.csv` — optional fallback for 2020 population.
5. `manila_barangay_elevation.csv` — required QGIS Zonal Statistics output containing barangay-level DTM elevation statistics.
6. `manila_barangay_district_mapping.csv` — district lookup for leave-one-district-out validation
   (read from backend/app/data/ if not in Input/).

Outputs Produced by the Pipeline (Output/)

Analytical datasets:
MetroManila_Barangay_Flood_Area_Validated.csv
manila-city-flood-population_enriched_NEW.csv / .xlsx
manila_ml_ready_dataset.csv - the 11 candidate predictors and the DPI class target

Dashboard file set (read by the backend):
barangay_flood_risk_predictions.csv
best_flood_risk_model_pipeline.joblib - server-side only; never serve to browsers
model_comparison_results.csv - RF/GB/MLP candidates plus parsimony baselines
                               (Model_Role, Eligible_For_Selection)
entropy_component_weights.csv
feature_importance_gradient_boosting.csv
feature_importance_random_forest.csv
permutation_feature_importance.csv
confusion_matrices.csv - held-out (n = 180) matrices for the 3 candidates, long format
                         (Model, Actual, Predicted, Count). Not written by the notebook;
                         restored from its saved cell output and verified by refitting
                         with the same split and hyperparameters.
chart_*.png - charts embedded in the backend's comprehensive PDF report

Predictor screen and robustness checks:
table13_correlation_matrix_11_predictors.csv
table14_vif_predictors.csv
predictor_screen_decision.csv
district_spatial_validation_results.csv - leave-one-district-out metrics

Diagnostics and audits:
dpi_component_class_summary.csv - summary table by Low/Medium/High
top_rank_explanation.csv - top 25 explanation table
high_dpi_medium_flood_audit.csv - explains exposure-driven high ranks
elevation_outlier_audit.csv - shows elevation anomalies
population_change_sensitivity_audit.csv - shows robustness checks

The correlation heatmap (figure_correlation_heatmap.png) is kept in reports/figures/.
